// frontend.jsonc: the browser client: its decisions, the copies it keeps, and the requirements its model is held to (an area part: items whose id starts fe-, d-fe- or copy-browser-).
// A part of the Strata specification; spec.jsonc lists the parts. Generated by scripts/split-spec.mjs
// the first time, edited in place after that. See specifications/README.md.
{
  "decisions": [
    {"id":"d-fe-1","ref":"D-FE-1","title":"The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**The browser cache is a stamped copy, and correctness never depends on it.** Every view result the web application keeps is stamped with the tenant epoch, the generation and the erasure epoch the gateway read it at, one stamp for the whole reply. It is drawn as current only while its stamp is the newest the browser has heard of, carried forward by notices that do not name it, and otherwise drawn labelled with its age. A missing or evicted entry is a read from the gateway, never an error, and every write is decided again by the server."},
    {"id":"d-fe-2","ref":"D-FE-2","title":"Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Three stores in the browser, each for one kind of content.** A service worker keeps only content named by its hash (the built files, the fonts, the parts of the tenant's interface definition) in the Cache API, and passes every other request through untouched; the bootstrapped page, which carries the session, is never stored. IndexedDB holds stamped view results, the write queue and the last manifest, encrypted per principal. The kernel worker's memory holds the hot set."},
    {"id":"d-fe-3","ref":"D-FE-3","title":"One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**One leader tab per principal, chosen with Web Locks.** Each tab keeps its own kernel worker. The worker holding the exclusive lock of the site and principal opens the socket and drains the write queue; the others hear notices on a BroadcastChannel and read the shared IndexedDB. A SharedWorker is not used: Chrome for Android only began shipping it in 2026 and Samsung Internet does not. Idempotency keys keep a queued write applied once if two tabs ever both send it."},
    {"id":"d-fe-4","ref":"D-FE-4","title":"Custom elements draw, the kernel decides","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Custom elements draw, the kernel decides.** Web Components are renderers of the view model: they hold no application state, take properties, and report what the person did as events the main thread turns into kernel messages. They render into the light DOM so that labels, ARIA references and the page's styles reach them; a control with no native element is form-associated through ElementInternals. Declarative Shadow DOM is not used, because nothing is rendered on the server and no markup is parsed (D18)."},
    {"id":"d-fe-5","ref":"D-FE-5","title":"Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Writes made offline are queued intents, decided again by the server.** A queued write holds the intent, the stamp of the record it was decided on (none for a create) and an idempotency key drawn once and stored with it. The leader sends it on reconnecting with expected-version and the key (D-6595); the server commits it only at that stamp, and answers a repeat of the key with the recorded outcome. A create whose first sending is older than the key's retention less one hour is not sent again: the person is asked to check."},
    {"id":"d-fe-6","ref":"D-FE-6","title":"What cannot be done offline","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**What cannot be done offline.** Only an operation whose contract allows queueing may be queued; by default none does. Sign-in, step-up and anything needing a fresh authentication (D-700), payments and plan changes, roles, members, invitations, sessions, passkeys and second factors, schema changes and the Impact Lab, and subject rights requests are never queued: offline, their controls say they need a connection. Sign-out works offline: it erases the browser's copy at once and tells the gateway on the next connection."},
    {"id":"d-fe-7","ref":"D-FE-7","title":"Data at rest is encrypted under a key the server can take away","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**Data at rest is encrypted under a key the server can take away.** The identity service keeps a random key share per principal and device and gives it only to a session of that principal. The worker derives a non-extractable AES-GCM key from it and keeps it in memory; it persists the key in IndexedDB only when the person keeps their work available offline on a device they mark as theirs, and a realm may forbid that. Sign-out, signing out every session, removing the principal and erasing it delete the share, which makes every copy the browser left unreadable."},
    {"id":"d-fe-8","ref":"D-FE-8","title":"An erasure epoch in every stamp","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**An erasure epoch in every stamp.** The browser holds opened values, so a key destruction (D-350), which raises no generation, would leave them current. The server raises a per-tenant erasure epoch at every key destruction and sends it with every reply, notice and heartbeat; on a new epoch the browser deletes every view result stamped with an older one."},
    {"id":"d-fe-9","ref":"D-FE-9","title":"No third-party code reaches the browser","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**No third-party code reaches the browser.** The QR code of an authenticator enrolment is drawn by an encoder of the web application's own, and the fonts are served from the site's own built files. Vite stays as the build tool; Playwright, axe and tsc stay as tools of development."},
    {"id":"d-fe-10","ref":"D-FE-10","title":"The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser","group":"Frontend","decided":"2026-11-21","statement":"**The kernel runs the interface scenarios without a browser.** A driver in Node runs the real kernel and the shell's view functions against the real gateway, interprets each uiScenario's steps against the drawn tree, and injects faults (lost replies, dropped sockets, reloads, a second tab) at the driver's boundary from a seed. Steps only a browser can answer (accessibility scans, cookies, screenshots, layout) run in Playwright."}
  ],
  "copies": [
    {"id":"copy-browser-view","name":"Browser view result","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":12,"unit":"hour","mechanism":"stamped with the tenant epoch, generation and erasure epoch of its reply; drawn as current only at the newest stamp the browser has heard of, carried forward by notices, and otherwise drawn labelled with its age; while offline, at most until the session would end unused (D-700)","source":"d-fe-1"},"erasure":{"point":"deletion of the principal's key share (sign-out, signing out every session, the principal removed or erased), a new erasure epoch at the next contact with the gateway, or the end of the session's lifetime, whichever comes first","bound":12,"unit":"hour","source":"d-fe-7"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"View results kept in IndexedDB by the web application, per site and principal, encrypted under the principal's device key (D-FE-7). Correctness never depends on it (D-FE-1)."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-queue","name":"Browser write queue","of":["tbl-records"],"fields":["object","id","version","data"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"per-principal","freshness":{"bound":24,"unit":"hour","mechanism":"a queued intent with its idempotency key and decided stamp, removed when the gateway answers it; a create is not resent once its first sending is older than the key's retention less one hour (D-6595)","source":"d-fe-5"},"erasure":{"point":"the gateway's answer, sign-out, or deletion of the principal's key share, which makes it unreadable","bound":14,"unit":"day","source":"d-fe-7"},"dependsOnAuthority":true,"description":"Writes the person made while offline, kept in IndexedDB encrypted under the principal's device key until the leader tab has sent them and the gateway has answered."},
    {"id":"copy-browser-interface","name":"Browser interface definition","of":["tbl-schema-history"],"heldBy":"web-application","scope":"shared","freshness":{"bound":"zero","mechanism":"each part is named by the hash of its content, so a changed part is a new entry; the manifest is read again on every schema notice","source":"d-8250"},"erasure":{"point":"dropped when the manifest no longer lists it, or when the browser evicts the site's storage"},"description":"The parts of the tenant's interface definition, kept by the service worker in the Cache API. They hold no personal field and no record data (D-8250)."}
  ],
  "claims": [
    {"id":"fe-001","kind":"requirement","statement":"The client cache model SHALL return a cached value as current only when it was read at the newest generation the client has heard of.","rationale":"A copy in the browser can lag the server; what it must never do is pass a stale value off as current.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_current_eq","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::run_coh"],"ref":"FE-001","area":"frontend","section":"The cache and its coherence","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-19","g-20"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-009","kind":"requirement","statement":"The client cache model SHALL return a cached value read at an older generation than the newest the client has heard of only labelled with the generation it was read at.","rationale":"Offline and while catching up, an older copy is still useful to read, as long as it says how old it is.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_stale_older","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::run_coh"],"ref":"FE-009","area":"frontend","section":"The cache and its coherence","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.read`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-19","g-20"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-002","kind":"requirement","statement":"After the receipt of a confirmed commit, the client cache model SHALL return the committed value for the written key while the client has heard of no later generation.","rationale":"A person who saves sees what they saved, not an older copy.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::read_after_commit","lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::receipt_read"],"ref":"FE-002","area":"frontend","section":"The cache and its coherence","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.put`","traces":["d-fe-1","g-206"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-003","kind":"requirement","statement":"The client cache model SHALL serve no value opened before a key destruction that raised the erasure epoch it is stamped with.","rationale":"The browser holds opened values, and a key destruction raises no generation (D-350), so the generation alone would keep an erased value current.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Cache.lean::epoch_stamp_erasure_safe"],"ref":"FE-003","area":"frontend","section":"Privacy at rest","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Cache.runEpoch`","traces":["d-fe-8","d-350","g-350"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-004","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the client privacy model, a value kept at rest for one principal SHALL open with no key the browser holds for another principal.","rationale":"Separation on a shared device rests on which keys are present, not on which partition the code chooses to open.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::no_cross_principal","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::served_own"],"ref":"FE-004","area":"frontend","section":"Privacy at rest","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.Opens`","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-005","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the client privacy model, no value a principal left at rest SHALL open in that browser after the principal signs out, in any later state.","rationale":"Sign-out on a shared device must leave nothing readable, even when deleting the stored data did not complete.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::signout_erases"],"ref":"FE-005","area":"frontend","section":"Privacy at rest","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (signOut)","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-006","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the client privacy model, after a session ends, a value its principal left at rest SHALL open only after a session of that same principal fetches its key share again.","rationale":"Queued work survives an expired session for its own author and for no one else.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::expire_locks","lean/Strata/Client/Privacy.lean::unlock_needs_own_session"],"ref":"FE-006","area":"frontend","section":"Privacy at rest","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Privacy.step` (expire, fetchKey)","traces":["d-fe-7","g-20","g-206"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-007","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the offline write model, a queued write SHALL be committed only while its record is at the stamp the write was decided on.","rationale":"A write decided offline on an old copy must not overwrite a change it never saw.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_ok_guard","lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_classes"],"ref":"FE-007","area":"frontend","section":"Offline writes","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-010","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the offline write model, a submission of a queued write that is not committed SHALL leave every record, its stamp and its value unchanged.","rationale":"A conflict, a refusal and a repeated key are reported to the person and change nothing.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::submit_not_ok_unchanged"],"ref":"FE-010","area":"frontend","section":"Offline writes","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.Srv.submit`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-6595","g-206"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-008","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the offline write model, a queued write SHALL be applied at most once, however often and by however many tabs it is sent, while the server keeps its idempotency key.","rationale":"Reloads, lost replies and a second tab resend queued writes; each must take effect once.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-008","area":"frontend","section":"Offline writes","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-fe-3","d-6595","g-206"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"},
    {"id":"fe-011","kind":"requirement","statement":"In the offline write model, a queued write that carries a record stamp SHALL be applied at most once even after the server forgets its idempotency key.","rationale":"An update or delete decided on a stamp cannot apply twice, because its first application moves the record off that stamp for good; only a create depends on the key being kept.","evaluate":{"method":"proof"},"check":"test","checkedBy":["lean/Strata/Client/Queue.lean::stamped_at_most_once"],"ref":"FE-011","area":"frontend","section":"Offline writes","lifecycle":"active","boundary":"b-13","boundaryDetail":"`Strata.Client.Queue.run`","traces":["d-fe-5","d-fe-3","d-6595","g-206"],"milestone":6,"realisation":"checked"}
  ]
}
